hokku-server (4.0.1~dev.15-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The preset dropdown now follows the catalog's own order (shipped defaults
    first) rather than whatever order the JSON encoder produced, which was
    alphabetical.
  * The three shipped pipeline defaults are now named presets ("General
    (default)", "Black & white (default)", "Faces (default)") and lead the
    dropdown. A fresh install previously displayed "Custom (your edits)" for all
    three, because the UI names the selected entry by matching against the
    preset catalog and the defaults were deliberately kept out of it — so
    nothing ever matched, and untouched settings looked edited.
  * Per-picture conversion overrides. Any image's details view can now pin its
    own dither pipeline and/or its own letterbox-fill limit, independently of
    the library-wide settings, and "Compare presets" renders several candidates
    for that one picture side by side to choose from. The comparison sweeps the
    palette LUT as well as the presets, because all three built-in presets share
    one LUT — so a picture that converts to the wrong colours cannot be fixed by
    picking a different preset. Setting an override re-converts only that
    picture. Overrides survive Clear Cache & Re-convert and a re-upload of the
    same filename.
  * The dither editor is now one component mounted four times rather than three
    hand-written copies plus a new one; the copies had already drifted (the B&W
    panel was missing the face keep-out overlay).
  * ImageConfig is parsed strictly everywhere: every field required, enum values
    checked, unknown keys rejected. Config-shape changes move to the AppConfig
    migration chain (v10), which completes older stored blobs once. Previously a
    misspelled knob was silently ignored on every load and an invalid lut_name
    was only caught inside a render worker, as a failed conversion.
  * Fixes a hot-reload race that let a retiring image manager write its stale
    snapshot over the live one's database. It cost only recomputable fields
    before; it would have cost the new per-picture settings.
  * Fixes dither previews ignoring the crop-to-fill setting: the preview always
    letterboxed while its face-box overlay was computed for a cropped canvas.
    Previews are also now bounded in concurrency.
  * Declares waitress in requirements.txt — recreating the venv as documented
    produced an environment where the server could not start.

 -- Dennis Fleurbaaij <mail@dennisfleurbaaij.com>  Sun, 02 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0500

hokku-server (4.0.1~dev.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Per-pipeline dither defaults are now measured rather than chosen. General
    and B&W move to Atkinson; general gains OKLAB adaptive-saturation and OKLAB
    dynamic-range compression; B&W gains OKLAB DRC; faces turn both chroma
    boosters off. Each is the best-scoring combination of algorithm x LUT x
    saturation space x DRC space x adaptive-vivid x serpentine over the test
    corpus for that pipeline. Existing installs keep their stored settings —
    this changes defaults only. See docs/dither_search.md.
  * Adds tools/dither_search.py (the search harness) and two freely-licensed
    lipstick portraits to images/test/, without which the artifact that
    motivated this could not be measured on photographs at all.

