hokku-server (4.0.1~dev.23-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * No server code changes. Appliance image fix: the board could not reboot
    with no USB cable attached. getty@.service has PID 1 itself open
    /dev/ttyGS0 around service stop (TTYReset/TTYVHangup/TTYVTDisallocate);
    opening a gadget tty with no host attached blocks uninterruptibly, so
    systemd wedged mid-shutdown with no message, no timeout and no journal
    until the hardware watchdog fired ten minutes later. Since a deployed
    appliance has no cable attached, this was the default case. Adds a drop-in
    disabling those three, and lowers RebootWatchdogSec from 10min to 60s so
    any wedged shutdown self-recovers. Known upstream: raspberrypi/linux#1929.

 -- Dennis Fleurbaaij <mail@dennisfleurbaaij.com>  Sat, 01 Aug 2026 10:16:02 -0500

hokku-server (4.0.1~dev.22-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * No server code changes. Appliance image fix: the last-resort on-SD swapfile
    documented in the image's memory policy was never actually present.
    dphys-swapfile was missing from 00-packages (and is not in pi-gen stage2),
    so the config step skipped itself and `systemctl enable` failed into
    `|| true` — every image shipped with zram as its only swap. Adds the
    package, makes both swap layers fail the build loudly if they cannot be
    configured, and orders zram after the swapfile so the swapfile is still
    available while zram is swapped off during shutdown.

 -- Dennis Fleurbaaij <mail@dennisfleurbaaij.com>  Thu, 30 Jul 2026 23:24:12 -0500

hokku-server (4.0.1~dev.21-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Deep-sleep oscillator-drift calibration. Screens learn their RC-oscillator
    error from the existing sleep-error signal and correct the armed timer, so
    they land on the scheduled slot instead of waking early and refreshing
    twice. Screen records are keyed by a stable server-assigned sid with name
    and MAC as secondary indexes, so calibration survives both rename and
    reflash; legacy name-keyed databases migrate on load. Responses carry
    X-Sleep-Cal-PPM / X-Sleep-Cal-N and screens send X-Screen-Mac.
    Firmware: huessen 1.2.20, seeed 1.2.4, bigme_f7 1.2.10.

 -- Dennis Fleurbaaij <mail@dennisfleurbaaij.com>  Thu, 30 Jul 2026 22:02:49 -0500

hokku-server (4.0.1~dev.20-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: the B&W and face image pipelines were silently collapsing onto the
    default pipeline on every load, so all three behaved identically. A config
    blob missing any single field reset that pipeline to the fallback preset,
    and the shipped config.json.example was missing clahe_keepout_feather —
    so every install ran the colour pipeline for B&W and face photos.
  * Config blobs now MERGE onto their pipeline's defaults instead of being
    reset wholesale, so a config predating a field keeps the tuning it does
    carry. Removes the _LENIENT_DEFAULTS table this made unnecessary.
  * The face pipeline default is tuned for skin again (gentler CLAHE 1.25,
    stronger/wider unsharp 130/1.2, Atkinson); the B&W default regains its
    harder CLAHE 2.25 and neutral saturation ceiling.
  * config.json.example is now generated from the code
    (python -m hokku.webserver.gen_example_config) with a test that fails if
    the checked-in file drifts.

